/*
one-bad-scene.fountain — a localisation fixture, CC0 1.0 Universal.

WHY IT EXISTS. docs/audits/2026-09-12-adversarial/writer-loop.md finding 13:
a defect concentrated in ONE scene did not appear anywhere in the triage a
writer acts on. This is the easiest possible localisation test — eleven
near-identical clean scenes plus one scene carrying fourteen exchanges of
"As you know, Boris" exposition — and before 2026-09-12 the ranked list was
saturated by act-shape checks that fire on nearly every short script while
scene 12 did not appear at all.

It is deliberately dull. Every clean scene is the same shape, so the only
thing that distinguishes scene 12 is the defect, and any ranking that finds
scene 12 has found the defect rather than a coincidence.

Written for this repository; released CC0 like data/screenplays/.
*/

